ir value."],"prof":["ROIC of 12% earns above the cost of capital of 8.5%, but the 3pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.38).","It runs a 36% gross margin and converts 8% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.60x.","ROE of 13% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.7x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.8% of revenue on R&D and 0.5% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 3.6x net debt to EBITDA ($264.0M of cash against $2.5B of debt), with interest covered 4.5x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -1.9% over 3 years, -6.0% over 5 years and -0.3% over 10 years, so the decline is easing, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 14%).","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 11.7% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -11.5% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.9x, 2.5% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 2, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 26.1% on average."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.5%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 7 purchases and 1 sale over the past year, net $30.6M bought.","It returns 6.5% a year to shareholders (4.4% in buybacks and 2.2% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 2.9% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 12 consecutive years, though it has been cut 2.0% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 10,000 employees, each generates about $446K of revenue, 1.2x the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 2.1% a year.","That works out to $37K of free cash flow per employee.","Compensation governance scores poorly (9/10, lower